---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About — Nasser’s Bites">
  <article class="narrow">
    <a class="back-link" href="/">← Back to Home</a>
    <p class="eyebrow">A little about this corner of the internet</p>

    <h1 class="page-title">Hello, curious mind.</h1>

    <p class="page-intro">
      I'm a pharmacist who enjoys asking questions about medicines,
      exploring the science behind everyday practice, and learning
      something new along the way.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Why Nasser’s Bites?</h2>
      <p>
        Some ideas deserve more than a passing thought, but not every
        idea needs a full-length article. This is my place to collect
        small explanations, useful references, unanswered questions,
        and connections worth exploring.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How I think about learning</h2>
      <p>
        I believe understanding grows when we break complicated topics
        into smaller pieces, question what we read, and connect new
        knowledge to what we already know.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="signature">
      <p>Small pieces. Open questions. A garden still growing.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
.back-link {
  margin-bottom: 45px;
}

section {
  margin-top: 65px;
}

h2 {
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-weight: 500;
  font-size: 36px;
  margin-bottom: 18px;
}

section p {
  font-size: 18px;
  line-height: 1.85;
  color: var(--text-body);
}

.signature {
  padding: 22px 26px;
  border-inline-start: 3px solid var(--accent);
  background: var(--surface);
}

.signature p {
  margin: 0;
  font-family: var(--font-serif);
  font-size: 22px;
}

@media (max-width: 700px) {
  h2 {
    font-size: 30px;
  }

  section p {
    font-size: 17px;
  }
}
</style>
